- TRAVEL: When the action involves travel or movement toward a destination, your mechanical_summary
  MUST include an estimate of travel time and distance based on Pathfinder 1e overland movement
  rules. Consider: base speed (the character sheet shows Speed), mount speed if applicable
  (light horse: 50 ft / ~48 miles per day; heavy horse: 40 ft / ~32 miles per day), terrain
  modifiers (road x1, trackless x0.75, difficult x0.5), and forced march rules. State how many
  hours of travel and roughly how far the player covers so the Ruling step can determine the
  new position.
- ENVIRONMENTAL HAZARDS: account for swim checks (DC varies by water conditions), climb checks
  (DC by surface), balance checks on narrow/slippery surfaces, and weather effects (visibility,
  movement penalties in heavy rain/snow).
- MOVEMENT IN DIFFICULT TERRAIN: each square of difficult terrain costs 2 squares of movement.
  Running and charging are not possible in difficult terrain unless the character has special
  abilities.
